// src/v4/std/verification.dag
//
// Scope: TestClaim schema — tests are data, not code. Imported design from v3.
// Anchor: THESIS.md "Tests are structural data" §348-368 + Self-hosting facet 3
//
// Owns:
//   - TestClaim { kind: AssertKind, label: String, input, expected }
//   - AssertKind = Equals | Diagnostic | Compiles | RoundTrips   (closed —
//     the complete assertion set. Tier1 = Compiles | Diagnostic; Tier2 =
//     Equals; the self-host / format fixed point = RoundTrips. NO "..." —
//     a 5th kind at fill-time is a substrate-extension STOP, not a silent
//     open enum.)
//   - Boundary/simulation does NOT add an AssertKind. A simulated external
//     dependency is generated Node bound into `input` (program ∘ generated
//     simulator) — see lens/testgen.dag simulator-generation arm. The
//     assertion shape stays one of the closed 4; only `input` changes.
//   - no hand-Rust tests; every test predicate IS a TestClaim instance
//
// Consumes:
//   - std/node.dag: Conj, Disj for claim shape
//   - std/diagnostic.dag: Diagnostic for failure mode
//   (String for label is the kernel-ambient String — no import)
//
// Status: scaffold — fill per TASKS.md T-3
// Brief: see BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md; this file's I/O contract is the immutable
// contract for the worker. Splitting this file requires explicit operator
// ratification (substrate extension = stop signal).


module v4.std.verification

